The summer movie season isn&#8217;t just at your local cineplex, but it&#8217;s also at your local Barnes & Noble with the retailer&#8217;s annual Criterion Collection summer sale.

On sale for 50% off list prices, B&N marked down every available Criterion Collection title on DVD, Blu-ray and 4K Ultra HD disc. If you&#8217;re looking to build out your media library, then now is the best time to save with prices starting at just $7.49 (was $14.99). But act fast and shop now, this sale is set to expire on Sunday (July 26).

Shop Criterion Collection 50% off Summer Sale at B&N

The Criterion Collection is one of the best resources for all sorts of &#8220;important classic and contemporary films,&#8221; per the home video distributor , physical media releases.

The company even has concert films, music documentaries and musicals, including This Is Spinal Tap , The Wiz starring Diana Ross and Michael Jackson , Martin Scorsese&#8217;s The Last Waltz , the David Bowie documentary Moonage Daydream , David Byrne’s American Utopia from director Spike Lee and much more.

Additionally, the Criterion Collection has other prestige releases, like Pee-Wee&#8217;s Big Adventure , Killers of the Flower Moon , The Princess Bride , No Country for Old Men , Pixar&#8217;s WALL-E and much more &#8212; all 50% off list prices.

